(    Gross Shortage = Target Stock Level - Available Inventory Position) Tj
T* (Rule 5.3: Minimum Order Quantity \(MOQ\) Constraint: The recommended order quantity must never be less than the Supplier Minimum Order Quantity \(MOQ\). If Gross Shortage < MOQ, the order quantity must be raised to MOQ.) Tj
T* (Rule 5.4: Pack Size / Lot Ceiling Rule: Order quantities must be rounded up to the nearest integer multiple of the Supplier Pack Size using ceiling division:) Tj
T* (    Final Recommended Quantity = ceil\(max\(Gross Shortage, MOQ\) / Pack Size\) * Pack Size) Tj
T* (Rule 5.5: Every replenishment recommendation must articulate its assumptions, detailing the target stock level, available inventory position, and lot sizing calculations.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (============================================================) Tj
T* (SECTION 6: Missing Data Handling, Interactive Prompts & Idempotency) Tj
T* (============================================================) Tj
T* (Rule 6.1: When essential data parameters?specifically Supplier Lead Time?are missing or null \(e.g., product P204\), the agent must not fabricate values. The agent must pause execution, transition to the "Ask" stage, and prompt the human operator for the verified lead time in days.) Tj
T* (Rule 6.2: Once the operator supplies the missing value, the agent resumes execution through the state machine.) Tj
T* (Rule 6.3: Idempotency Key Registration: To eliminate duplicate order submissions during network retries or identical re-evaluations, every generated replenishment plan must be registered with a unique Plan ID, timestamp, and a cryptographic/hash idempotency key based on \(product_id, location, target_stock_level, as_of_date\).) Tj
T* (Rule 6.4: If a duplicate plan request is processed, the system must recognize the existing idempotency key and return the original Plan ID and plan record without creating a duplicate.) Tj
ET
